From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zerogap <zerogap@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:30:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] QRDetector: no line through two equal alignment pattern
 positions

SampleQR guesses a missing alignment pattern where the lines through its
neighbours meet. Two of those positions can be the same point (in a
damaged or crafted symbol); the line through them is not valid, and
intersect() asserts that both lines are. Found by fuzzing: an assertion
reached from a camera image. Skip the guess then, as when fewer than two
neighbours are known.
---
 core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp b/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp
index 9b4cdbfd..05e2c830 100644
--- a/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp
+++ b/core/src/qrcode/QRDetector.cpp
@@ -587,7 +587,8 @@ DetectorResults SampleQR(const BitMatrix& image, const FinderPatternSet& fp)
 				}
 
 				// if we found 2 each, intersect the two lines that are formed by connecting the point pairs
-				if (Size(hori) == 2 && Size(verti) == 2) {
+				// (two different points each: a line through one point is not valid)
+				if (Size(hori) == 2 && Size(verti) == 2 && hori[0] != hori[1] && verti[0] != verti[1]) {
 					auto guessed = intersect(RegressionLine(hori[0], hori[1]), RegressionLine(verti[0], verti[1]));
 					auto found = LocateAlignmentPattern(image, estimateModuleSize(x, y), guessed);
 					// search again near that intersection and if the search fails, use the intersection
